      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The subdivision was officially established in 1964, placing it among the early wave of modern residential developments on Hawaiʻi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bigalohaguide.com/places/leilani-estates",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Leilani Estates sits directly on the lower East Rift Zone of Kīlauea, a lava flow hazard zone 1 where new vents can erupt anywhere.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leilani_Estates%2C_Hawaii",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the 2018 lower Puna eruption, about 200 homes were destroyed within Leilani Estates as lava flowed toward the ocean.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leilani_Estates%2C_Hawaii",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In January 2019, the Leilani Community Association began enforcing rules against parking on private roads and trespassing to keep the subdivision private.",
